{
  "title": "Apollo",
  "year": "2024",
  "text": "Designed by Victor Pasmore and completed in 1969, the Apollo Pavilion in Peterlee is a reinforced concrete sculpture and bridge. Its interlocking blocks connect the geometry of the estate’s curving roads and box-shaped houses. As you move around it, the concrete forms seem to rotate and shift, changing the shape you see from each new angle.",
